@startuml
title Purchase Request Workflow — Single-Service Deployment View
skinparam shadowing false

node "User device" as Client {
  artifact "Browser" as Browser
}

node "Application host" as Host {
  node "One FastAPI application process" as App {
    component "HTTP + static UI" as HTTP
    component "Application/domain modules" as Core
    component "Run-scoped in-memory EventBus" as EventBus
    component "Persistence adapters" as Persistence
  }
}

database "SQLite\nworkflow.db" as Database

Browser --> HTTP : client-server requests
HTTP --> Core : in-process use cases
Core --> EventBus : in-process choreography triggers
Core --> Persistence : transactions and queries
Persistence --> Database : definitions, purchase requests, runs,\napprovals, attempts, notifications, trace

note right of App
Orchestration and choreography share this process.
Restart recovery reads persistent cursors.
EventBus holds no waiting state.
end note

note "Absent: Kafka, ZooKeeper, distributed broker,\nmicroservices, external workflow engine,\npayment/accounting system, external email." as Exclusions

legend
Local start and Docker Compose use the same single-service boundary.
Runtime files are persistent data and are not tracked by Git.
endlegend
@enduml
